            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery aneurysms after angioplasty and atherectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1030-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery aneurysm formation after percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty and directional coronary atherectomy is unusual. We report the case of a left anterior descending coronary artery aneurysm that formed in such a patient. The left anterior descending coronary artery was bypassed and the aneurysm was plicated with the aid of coronary angioscopy. The English-language medical literature on the topic of coronary artery aneurysms is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
